Aerie-Purpose: Cap the reported device memory (navigator.deviceMemory, workers, Device-Memory and Sec-CH-Device-Memory) at 8 GB on desktop, so a machine with more memory looks like the common 8 GB one.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/common/device_memory/approximated_device_memory.cc (ApproximatedDeviceMemory::CalculateAndSetApproximatedDeviceMemory)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Upstream clamps the value to 2..32 GB on desktop (crbug.com/454354290 raised the top
from 8 to 32) and to 1..8 GB on Android. This patch sets the desktop top to 8 while the
HeliumNoise feature is enabled. One edit covers navigator.deviceMemory in windows and
workers and both client hint headers, because they all read the same cached value.

The cap follows the HeliumNoise feature only. It does not read the helium.noise.enabled
pref or the per-site HELIUM_NOISE content setting, so it stays at 8 when fingerprinting
protection is turned off, globally or for one site. This is the one exception to "off
restores the real value", decided in issue #115: a site that sees the real 32 learns
something about the machine and helps nobody. There is no farbling. A machine with less
than 8 GB keeps its real bucket (the lower clamp of 2 GB is unchanged). Starting the
browser with --disable-features=HeliumNoise lifts the cap; the Bench uses that as its
negative control.

--- a/third_party/blink/common/device_memory/approximated_device_memory.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/common/device_memory/approximated_device_memory.cc
@@ -71,6 +71,15 @@
     kMaxMemory = 8.0f;
 #endif
 
+  // Aerie: cap at 8 GB on desktop too. Machines with more memory are rare, so
+  // a larger value only tells a site more about this one. This follows the
+  // HeliumNoise feature alone, not the fingerprinting pref or the per-site
+  // switch: like the reduced user agent, it is a normalisation that stays on
+  // when the noise is turned off.
+  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kHeliumNoise)) {
+    kMaxMemory = 8.0f;
+  }
+
   if (approximated_device_memory_gb_ < kMinMemory) {
     approximated_device_memory_gb_ = kMinMemory;
   } else if (approximated_device_memory_gb_ > kMaxMemory) {
